    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hello folks!\r\nI've been thinking about using this plugin but I'd love to be able to actually setup automatic trim on write with confirmation. This would only make sense if there were actually any trailing whitespaces/lines on the buffer.\r\n\r\nI managed to set an autocmd but I couldn't figure out how to check if there were trailing whitespaces on the buffer. I'd guess I could do the same check myself but It'd be great if I could use anything in the module to check that instead of rewriting some of the logic.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"BufWritePre\" }, {\r\n    callback = function()\r\n        vim.fn.confirm(\"Trim Whitespaces? [Y/n]\", \"&y\\n&n, 1)\r\n        -- Conditional to check the option (Didn't do it since I was focusing on the trigger first\r\n        -- if choice == 1then\r\n       --    require(\"mini.trailspace\").trim()\r\n       --    require(\"mini.trailspace\").trim_last_lines()\r\n```\r\n\r\nThanks (=",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hello folks!<br>\nI've been thinking about using this plugin but I'd love to be able to actually setup automatic trim on write with confirmation. This would only make sense if there were actually any trailing whitespaces/lines on the buffer.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I managed to set an autocmd but I couldn't figure out how to check if there were trailing whitespaces on the buffer. I'd guess I could do the same check myself but It'd be great if I could use anything in the module to check that instead of rewriting some of the logic.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ &quot;BufWritePre&quot; }, {\n    callback = function()\n        vim.fn.confirm(&quot;Trim Whitespaces? [Y/n]&quot;, &quot;&amp;y\\n&amp;n, 1)\n        -- Conditional to check the option (Didn't do it since I was focusing on the trigger first\n        -- if choice == 1then\n       --    require(&quot;mini.trailspace&quot;).trim()\n       --    require(&quot;mini.trailspace&quot;).trim_last_lines()\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>({ <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>BufWritePre<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>}, {\n    <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n        <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fn</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">confirm</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>Trim Whitespaces? [Y/n]<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&amp;y<span class=\"pl-cce\">\\n</span>&amp;n, 1)</span>\n        <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Conditional to check the option (Didn't do it since I was focusing on the trigger first</span>\n        <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> if choice == 1then</span>\n       <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span>    require(\"mini.trailspace\").trim()</span>\n       <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span>    require(\"mini.trailspace\").trim_last_lines()</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks (=</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hello folks!\nI've been thinking about using this plugin but I'd love to be able to actually setup automatic trim on write with confirmation. This would only make sense if there were actually any trailing whitespaces/lines on the buffer.\nI managed to set an autocmd but I couldn't figure out how to check if there were trailing whitespaces on the buffer. I'd guess I could do the same check myself but It'd be great if I could use anything in the module to check that instead of rewriting some of the logic.\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"BufWritePre\" }, {\n    callback = function()\n        vim.fn.confirm(\"Trim Whitespaces? [Y/n]\", \"&y\\n&n, 1)\n        -- Conditional to check the option (Didn't do it since I was focusing on the trigger first\n        -- if choice == 1then\n       --    require(\"mini.trailspace\").trim()\n       --    require(\"mini.trailspace\").trim_last_lines()\nThanks (=",
